From e492d0c4a748149054f8cc2623846a1c1da3b0c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:59:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: one line in the log for each seek

Without debug logging Kodi says nothing of a seek, and the gaps that seeks
leave are read as stalls. In the hardware test of 1.0 RC4 the native Dolby
Vision statistics of the AMD integrated graphics showed gaps of 500.8 and
542.2 ms that were the user's seeks; nothing in kodi.log could tell.

The player now tells the render manager of each seek it handled (not the
seeks of trick play): where the playback was, where it was asked to go, where
the stream got to, when the player began and when it was done (the stream
sought and the buffers flushed). Frames carry the number they were added to
the render queue with; the first frame added after the player was done that
is chosen for the screen ends the seek, and its line is written then:

  Seek: from 00:41:12.345 to 00:45:00.000: the player began 2 ms after it
  was asked for and had the stream at 00:44:58.120 642 ms later; the first
  frame after it went to the screen 1210 ms after it was asked for

A seek without a frame after it is told when the next one is handled or when
the playback of the file ends. A seek that the player leaves out (a stream
that cannot seek, an inaccurate seek while the video of the one before is not
in sync yet) says so. The logic is in SeekTrace.h, with a host test.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDMessage.h           |   8 +
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/SeekTrace.h            | 138 ++++++++++++++++++
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp        |  24 +++
 .../VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp          |  37 +++++
 .../VideoRenderers/RenderManager.h            |  12 ++
 5 files changed, 219 insertions(+)
